   "question": "How is a station selected for bike delivery?",
   "question_id": "q01",
   "rag": {
    "answer": "A station is selected for bike delivery when its available bikes fall to or below the low\u2011bike threshold, at which point it enters the rebalancing queue. Dispatchers then prioritize stations by the sum of severity points, deficit points, and station\u2011size points, choosing the highest\u2011scoring station first while checking nearby stations and current telemetry. If both bikes and docks are critically low, the action is **INSPECT STATION** rather than an automatic delivery. Out\u2011of\u2011service stations are excluded from this process. [4][3]",
